Subject: Name for a Dalmatian

A good name for an Extropian Dalmatian would be,

        Diffusion/Reaction   (D/R for short).

This is the name of a model for the process that
gives rise to spots, stripes and such on animals'
coats.  The theory is that various chemical signals spread from cell to
neighboring cell in the skin as it develops, and then combinations of
levels of different signals trigger reactions in the cells, which
then send out different signals depending, etc.

It's a famous form of spontaneous order.  The exact spot pattern isn't
programmed into the genes, but arises from interactions of the cells.

And Diffusion/Reaction also makes a nice Extropian sentiment:
spreading out and interacting.

[I can look up a reference to the Scientific American article,
"How the Leopard Gets its Spots," if anyone would like.  I got a
little book of reprints, with the same title, when I renewed my
subscription recently.]

